---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CaseHeader from '../../components/CaseHeader.astro';
import SessionFlow from '../../components/SessionFlow.astro';
import {projectRecords} from '../../data/portfolio';
import {sessionbookMeta} from '../../data/sessionbook';
const title='SessionBook — Booking backend for a voice agent | Stephen Mensah';
const description=projectRecords.sessionbook.summary;
const structuredData={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'CreativeWork',name:'SessionBook',description,url:new URL('/work/sessionbook/',Astro.site).href,author:{'@type':'Person',name:'Stephen Mensah'},about:{'@type':'SoftwareSourceCode',codeRepository:sessionbookMeta.repoUrl}};
---
<BaseLayout {title} {description} {structuredData} ogType="article"><article><CaseHeader id="sessionbook" sections={[{id:'primer',label:'The problem'},{id:'architecture',label:'Booking flow'},{id:'boundary',label:'Result & limits'}]}/><div class="page-shell">
 <section id="primer" class="case-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">The problem</p><h2>The conversation<br />can be flexible.<br />The booking can’t.</h2></div><div class="case-section__body"><p>A voice agent can ask a caller what time works. It shouldn’t decide whether a slot exists, whether someone else just booked it, or whether a confirmation is valid.</p><p>I built the FastAPI service behind that boundary: typed HTTP tools, availability queries, a transaction around booking, and responses designed to be read aloud.</p><aside class="boundary"><p><strong>Implementation verified, calls unverified.</strong> {projectRecords.sessionbook.boundary}</p></aside></div></section>
 <section id="architecture" class="case-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">One inspector</p><h2>From request<br />to read-back.</h2><p class="muted">Open any step. No backend connection is made by this view.</p></div><div class="case-section__body" id="trace"><span id="call-path"></span><SessionFlow/></div></section>
 <span id="evidence"></span><section id="boundary" class="case-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">Result & limits</p><h2>Written is a state.<br />Proven is another.</h2></div><div class="case-section__body"><p>{projectRecords.sessionbook.result}</p><div class="compare-grid"><div class="compare-sheet"><h3 id="sb-known-title">Present in source</h3><ul><li>Four mounted POST /tools routes</li><li>AssemblyAI agent configuration and creation script</li><li>SELECT … FOR UPDATE and unique slot constraint</li><li>Provider timezone: Africa/Accra</li><li>Phone normalization and 7–15 digit validation</li><li>Speakable confirmation and conflict responses</li></ul></div><div class="compare-sheet"><h3 id="sb-missing-title">Needs verification</h3><ul><li>Live voice or phone calls</li><li>Deployment and operational behaviour</li><li>Concurrent database execution tests</li><li>Empty tests/test_booking.py</li><li>No generated Alembic migration versions</li><li>Latency, reliability and usage outcomes</li></ul></div></div><details id="questions"><summary>Source, reference & remaining concerns</summary><p>Re-inspected at commit 1264d9e. The source supports integration code, not an independently verified end-to-end call. README setup instructions and an agent ID file do not establish deployment.</p><p>The service validates normalized phone numbers; the earlier portfolio claim that short numbers were still accepted was stale. Tool authentication and production readiness still need review.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${sessionbookMeta.repoUrl}/tree/1264d9e`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Inspect pinned source ↗</a><br/><a class="text-link" href={sessionbookMeta.tutorialUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Conceptual reference: AssemblyAI tutorial ↗</a></details></div></section>
 <a class="next-project" href="/work/koranco/"><span><span class="eyebrow">Next project</span><strong>Koranco Farms</strong></span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
 </div></article></BaseLayout>
